  "query_preview": "..\n(Saturday through next Wednesday)\nIssued at 114 PM CDT Thu Aug 20 2026\n\nHeat continues into early next week and Monday may be the hottest \nday of the period for some (including AMA) per the NBM. The H5 high \ncenter is forecast by current operational runs of the GEM, ECMWF and \nGFS to retreat WSW by mid-week which allows modest decrease in temps \ntoward the end of the forecast period. More importantly this brings \nNW flow and upper level s/wvs back into the fold and there are \nenough favorable ensemble members for storms that the NBM is showing \nsolid chc/sct POPs (30-60% - favoring NW) each evening from \nTuesday through Thursday. Of course, this was the cast last week \nfor the middle of this week and the ridge ended up holding strong,\nso we will remain cautiously optimistic wrt this subtle but \nimportant pattern change.\n\nGittinger",
